# C · CONTEXT

## 1. The product
FairShift is a workforce platform that makes work **fairer, safer, and more transparent** in employee-intensive organisations. It gives workers clarity and a voice, and gives employers actionable insight into workforce health. It is aligned to UN SDG 8 (Decent Work and Economic Growth).

## 2. The problem
Large workforces still run on paper registers, spreadsheets, and WhatsApp groups. Sectors affected: **Construction** (daily shift workers), **Colleges and Schools** (campus and facility staff), **Hospitals** (round-the-clock care and sanitation teams), **Factories** (floor and line operators).

| Who | Problems today |
|---|---|
| Workers | Opaque pay and uncounted overtime · fear of being identified when complaining or giving feedback · hazards ignored until injuries occur · lost career history because skills go unrecorded |
| Employers | No view of overworked or unhappy staff · cannot spot people likely to quit · issues reach management only once severe |
| Accessibility | Workers speak regional languages · many have limited literacy, so voice and visual cues are essential · most use basic, low-end smartphones |

## 3. Required deliverables
1. At least **3 working features** in a functional prototype (custom ideas welcome).
2. **Two distinct interfaces**: one for workers, one for employers/admins.
3. At least **2 industry use cases**, with a short explanation of cross-sector adoption (for example, a construction site and a college).

## 4. Success criteria (the finished app is judged on these)
| # | Criterion | Meaning for the app |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Real-world impact | Tangible improvement to worker safety and employer visibility |
| 2 | Relevance to SDG 8 | Direct alignment with decent work and economic growth |
| 3 | Inclusivity and ease of use | Regional languages, low literacy, basic phones |
| 4 | Technical implementation | Clean code, security, two working interfaces |
| 5 | Feasibility and scalability | Practical adoption across two or more industries |

## 5. Why customisation is a core requirement
No two workplaces run alike. A construction site pays daily wages with gate-based check-in; a college pays monthly salaries to teaching and support staff on different shift patterns. The app must adapt by **configuration, never by editing code**. Three kinds of people must be able to customise it:

| Layer | Who | How | Examples |
|---|---|---|---|
| A | Organisation admin | Settings screens, no coding | Pay rules, thresholds, terminology, workflows, dashboards |
| B | Worker | Personal settings | Language, text size, contrast, simple mode, voice, home screen |
| C | Developer | Adding files | New language, sector preset, hazard set, feature module |

